# Environment — .venv is the macOS/Linux one, .venv-win the Windows one.
# They cannot share a directory (bin/ vs Scripts/, platform-specific binaries),
# and this project folder syncs through OneDrive between both machines.
.venv/
.venv-win/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/

# Data — never commit the dataset or derived artefacts
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet
data/*.npz
data/rule_hits.csv    # per-account scenario codes (regenerated by Stage 9)          # out-of-fold SHAP matrix (regenerated by Stage 4/5)
data/*.xlsx
!data/.gitkeep
# The hackathon file is often dropped in the project root instead of data/
/DataSet*.csv
/Description.xlsx

# Models & reports (regenerated by the pipeline).
# 00_INTEGRITY.md is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the finding that frames
# every metric in this project and should travel with the repository.
models/*.joblib
reports/*.png
reports/*.json
!reports/00_INTEGRITY.md

# OS
.DS_Store

# Per-dataset workdirs created by MULEGUARD_WORKDIR
runs/
data/alien_dataset.csv

# Alert exports — these are NOT anonymous. `entity_ref` is the row index into
# the supplied dataset, so anyone holding that file (the bank, the organisers,
# other teams) can join on it and recover exactly which customers were flagged.
# The exports carry real feature values plus "freeze / prepare STR" outcomes for
# 105 real accounts, which is an accusation record, not a demo artefact.
# integration_contract.json is the field schema only and is safe to publish.
reports/exports/alerts.*
reports/exports/case_pack_*.json

# The paper. v3_current is THE deliverable and is tracked; the *backup* files
# are local undo points from editing sessions and stay out of the repository.
reports/*backup*.docx

# The organisers' LaTeX template, already vendored under paper/
/Prototype_Template_CyberShield/

# Blind hold-out: 1,506 real feature values for 213 real customers, 13 of them
# labelled as mules, keyed by row_number back into the supplied dataset. Same
# reasoning as reports/exports/alerts.csv - it is joinable, so it identifies
# people. Regenerate locally with src/make_blind_holdout.py.
reports/blind_holdout/
